# Chaudron PWA — build-time configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Every VITE_* value is INLINED INTO THE
# JAVASCRIPT BUNDLE at build time and is therefore public — and, because the
# service worker precaches the bundle, it is copied onto every visitor's device.
# Never put a secret, an API key, a provider token or anything that grants
# access here.
#
# There used to be a VITE_HOUSEHOLD_ID in this file, and it was the whole of the
# application's access control. It was published with every build: the real UUID
# sat in clear text in `dist/assets/index-*.js`, so loading the page was enough
# to read it and then use it from `curl` — CORS being a browser rule that no
# command-line client has ever obeyed. It is gone. The active household is now
# runtime state derived from the signed-in session, and the server verifies
# membership on every request.

# Base URL of the Chaudron API — OPTIONAL, and best left unset.
#
# The client defaults to the origin the page was served from, so the ordinary
# deployment needs nothing here. That default is not a convenience: the session
# cookie is `__Host-` prefixed and `SameSite=Lax`, so the API has to be same-site
# with the page or the cookie is never sent, and the documented setup puts both
# behind one reverse proxy on one origin. Deriving it from the page is the
# arrangement the cookie already requires.
#
# Set it ONLY for the one supported layout the default cannot express:
# `api.example.org` beside `app.example.org` — same registrable domain, different
# origin. Setting it inlines that hostname into the JavaScript bundle, which
# makes the build specific to one instance and is exactly what the published
# container image exists to avoid.
#
# Without a trailing slash and without `/v1` (the client appends `/v1/...`
# itself). Anywhere but localhost it must be `https://`: browsers accept `Secure`
# cookies from `localhost` and `127.0.0.1` over plain HTTP, so the local loop
# works as-is.
#VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Public site URL, used for `<link rel=canonical>`, Open Graph and sitemap.xml.
#
# A production build without it FAILS rather than guessing — a wrong canonical
# points every crawler at somebody else's domain and nothing reports it.
#
# Three ways to satisfy it:
#   VITE_SITE_URL=https://chaudron.example.tld   the ordinary one
#   VITE_DEFER_SITE_URL=1                        leave `__SITE_URL__` in place
#                                                for the deployment to fill in;
#                                                this is how the published image
#                                                is built
#   VITE_ALLOW_DEFAULT_SITE_URL=1                local builds only, never deploy
#VITE_SITE_URL=
